{
  "pr": {
    "number": 164,
    "title": "fix(mcp): honor Windows client profiles and shim commands",
    "body": "Windows user-scoped MCP installs can fall back to the current directory when HOME is absent and miss clients installed as .exe/.cmd/.bat files. This change resolves explicit paths, client overrides and the native Windows profile in order, then shares pinned executable discovery and command context across registration, same-target file fallback and visibility. Relative overrides retain their target when child CWD changes; both Claude project spellings keep their .mcp.json list check.\n\nRefs [COD-55](https://linear.app/codebasegraph/issue/COD-55), CBG-PLAT-01/S04 R04/A07\u2013A08 only. Fresh-main base: `9557b3806ce46cb1acadd95cfbf712c07ea8556d` (4.0.1). [Approved spec rev0.11](https://github.com/rabii-chaarani/codebaseGraph/blob/8a410c7a22f5291f06a1cece5cd9e7c0be255e72/docs/specs/CBG-PLAT-01/spec.md#s04--use-explicit-windows-user-directory-and-executable-discovery-policy); [exact approval](https://github.com/rabii-chaarani/codebaseGraph/blob/949db168fcf128cc1fe6e73cb70a14db832d50b5/docs/specs/CBG-PLAT-01/approvals/cod55-windows-client-discovery.md). Published canonical spec/evidence is imported unchanged because main lacked it. Scryer: chg-7vkjtj; cfg-only warning hygiene: chg-y5ahjy.\n\nCorrected product revision: `84cdb27386ea4d86166135d82736a62deb2bd1ba`.\n\n- Final affected macOS suite: **58/58 pass**, zero selected cases skipped; fmt and strict workspace/all-target/all-feature Clippy pass.\n- Windows-target isolated helper/fixture type check and strict Clippy pass; not native execution.\n- Fresh Sol High proposal and Sol Max integrated/focused source reviews pass with no remaining confirmed P0\u2013P3.\n- [Native CI40616153340](https://github.com/rabii-chaarani/codebaseGraph/actions/runs/40616153340) is running for the corrected source. Earlier CI40613075649 caught a test-fixture private API call; corrected without widening the API. Four preexisting Windows warnings were resolved with reviewed platform guards. Failed attempts remain in the evidence.\n\nActual Windows argv/shim/configuration execution and complete native CI remain pending. Windows Server CI does not establish Windows 11 desktop consumer qualification. The original-checkout Scryer binding cannot record this isolated branch's test fingerprints; exact revision-bound evidence is retained with the canonical spec. COD-55 and aggregate closure remain open; no merge, release publication, deployment or restart is requested.",
